{
  "name": "W01 · Case-clock tick (08:00 IST) → API-65 → Render Workflows case_clock_sweep",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 0 8 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "a1f0c001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Every day 08:00 IST",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [0, 300],
      "notes": "Workflow timezone = Asia/Kolkata (see settings). Render Workflows has no cron trigger, so n8n starts the sweep (D-15, D-16). 08:00 is after quiet hours (22:00–07:00 IST, MD-130)."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Build and sign the API-65 request. Reshapes JSON only; no business logic (D-16).\n// Margdarshak-Signature: t=<unix>,v1=<hex HMAC-SHA256(secret, t + '.' + body)>\n// (same scheme as services/api/internal/platform/hmacsig). The API rejects |now - t| > 300 s and\n// any signature it has seen before, so every attempt (including retries) is signed afresh here.\nconst crypto = require('crypto');\nconst runDate = $now.setZone('Asia/Kolkata').toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd');\nconst body = JSON.stringify({\n  sweep_id: `sweep-${runDate}-0800`,\n  as_of: new Date().toISOString(), // advisory: the API uses its own server date (EC-15)\n  dry_run: false,\n});\nconst ts = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000).toString();\nconst v1 = crypto.createHmac('sha256', $vars.MD_HMAC_SECRET).update(`${ts}.${body}`).digest('hex');\nreturn [{ json: { body, signature: `t=${ts},v1=${v1}`, idempotency_key: `case-clock:${runDate}`, run_date: runDate } }];"
      },
      "id": "a1f0c001-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Build + sign sweep request (HMAC)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [220, 300],
      "notes": "Needs the built-in `crypto` module in Code nodes (allowed on n8n Cloud; self-hosted: NODE_FUNCTION_ALLOW_BUILTIN=crypto)."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $vars.MD_API_BASE }}/internal/clock/sweep",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Authorization",
              "value": "=Bearer {{ $vars.MD_N8N_READ_TOKEN }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Margdarshak-Signature",
              "value": "={{ $json.signature }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Idempotency-Key",
              "value": "={{ $json.idempotency_key }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "raw",
        "rawContentType": "application/json",
        "body": "={{ $json.body }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": true,
              "neverError": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "a1f0c001-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "API-65 start sweep",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [440, 300],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "notes": "POST /internal/clock/sweep (API-65). The API verifies the HMAC, fixes as_of to its own IST date and starts the Render Workflows task `case_clock_sweep` ({WORKFLOW_SLUG}/case_clock_sweep, services/workflows) through the JobRunner port. 202 → JobRun { job, run_id, runner, status, idempotent_replay }. Idempotent per run date. No built-in retry here: a retry must be re-signed, so failures loop back through the signing node."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c-accepted",
              "leftValue": "={{ Number($json.statusCode) >= 200 && Number($json.statusCode) < 300 }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1f0c001-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Sweep accepted (2xx)?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [660, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "a1f0c001-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Sweep started (delivery via W02)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [880, 200],
      "notes": "Done. The sweep runs on Render Workflows: clock.plan_pages → clock_batch ×K (≤ 8 concurrent) → clock.fire_batch. For each batch the API POSTs the due messages (signed envelope) to W02's webhook `md/milestone`, which sends WhatsApp/email and acks receipts on API-66. Progress: Render Runs page and ops.job_runs."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c-retryable",
              "leftValue": "={{ $runIndex < 2 && (!$json.statusCode || Number($json.statusCode) === 429 || Number($json.statusCode) >= 500) }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1f0c001-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Retryable (network/429/5xx, < 3 tries)?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [880, 420]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "amount": 10,
        "unit": "seconds"
      },
      "id": "a1f0c001-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "name": "Wait 10 s",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [1100, 340],
      "webhookId": "5c1d7c2e-0d0a-4b0e-9c61-0a01a0010001",
      "notes": "Back-off before re-signing (same Idempotency-Key, fresh timestamp and signature)."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "errorMessage": "=Case-clock sweep was not started: HTTP {{ $json.statusCode || 'network error' }} {{ ($json.body && $json.body.title) || $json.error?.message || '' }}. Runbook: docs/05-ops/RUNBOOK.md#pb-08"
      },
      "id": "a1f0c001-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "name": "Fail → W12 alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stopAndError",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1100, 520]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Every day 08:00 IST": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Build + sign sweep request (HMAC)",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Build + sign sweep request (HMAC)": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "API-65 start sweep",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
